--- Shader_09_FBM/storyboard/before
+++ Shader_09_FBM/storyboard/after
@@ -1 +1 @@
-The student crosses the glass above the basin, then studies the layered noise panels. They bring weighted field sums and a working fragment shader, and make a finite octave loop that retains frequency and amplitude as separate running values. They map its result into colour, producing a material they can apply to another supplied surface. The base noise function, panel material and basin assembly are supplied. The glass bears the visitor while water moves beneath it; its existing displacement remains supplied, so this lesson deepens field composition without silently introducing the vertex-shader stage.
+The student crosses the glass above the moving basin, then returns to the noise panels with the form function they have kept. Noise and weighted sums are familiar; here a finite shader loop combines a few scales with separate frequency and amplitude updates. A bounded contribution disturbs the mask’s boundary while the panel mesh stays fixed. Compare no disturbance with the chosen amount before adding time. The student changes the finest contribution while retaining the broad form and explains the difference. They carry a field function and its range. The basin’s vertex displacement and normal construction are supplied comparisons: its surface moves, but the glass is what carries the visitor.
--- Shader_09_FBM/storyboard_short/before
+++ Shader_09_FBM/storyboard_short/after
@@ -1 +1 @@
-Use layered panels and glass above moving water. Reuse weighted fields and fragment shader. Teach finite octave accumulation with separate frequency/amplitude values, then colour mapping. Supply base noise, panel material and basin assembly, including water displacement and normals. Carry reusable layered material. Glass supplies support; the water material supplies no collision. Defer vertex-stage teaching.
+Use noise panels and glass-covered basin. Reuse mask, weighted sums and Noise. Teach bounded octave loop; keep frequency/amplitude separate. Perturb mask boundary; compare zero contribution before adding time. Check: change fine detail while retaining broad form. Carry field + range. Supply base noise/material host and basin displacement/normals. Glass supplies support. Defer vertex teaching; coordinate warp optional.
--- Shader_12_PinkExtravaganza/title/before
